#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100575 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "0713e68d-2b3e-5010-954f-7891d96bdbbb" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3640" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-1$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $h(x)$ | $z(x)$ | $h'(x)$ | $z'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $-1$ | $-4$ | $2$ | $6$ | $3$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right)$ at $x=-1$." :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right) = \\dfrac{h'(x)z(x)-h(x)z'(x)}{(z(x))^2}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}((h(x))/(z(x))) \\mid _{x =-1} &= (h^{′}(-1)z(-1) - h(-1)z^{′}(-1))/((z(-1))^{2}) \\\\\n&= (6 \\cdot 2 - (-4) \\cdot 3)/(2^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{24}{4} \\\\\n&= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100576 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "787e9681-8009-5ba8-acda-6d8830397d18" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3641" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, we have\n$f(1)=2, \\quad f'(1)=2, \\quad g(1)=-1, \\quad g'(1)=3$.\nIf $h(x) = \\left(f(x)-1 \\right)\\left(2g(x)+1\\right)$, compute $h'(1)$." :question/worked-solution "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big(uv\\Big) = u \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} +v \\dfrac{\\textrm du}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nLet $u=f(x)-1$ and\n\n$$\nv=2g(x)+1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = f'(x) \\qquad \\text{and}\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} = 2g'(x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nh^{′}(x) &= u\\frac{dv}{dx} + v\\frac{du}{dx} \\\\\n&= (f(x) - 1) \\cdot 2g^{′}(x) + (2g(x) + 1) \\cdot f^{′}(x) \\\\\n&= 2g^{′}(x)(f(x) - 1) + f^{′}(x)(2g(x) + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nh^{′}(1) &= 2g^{′}(1)(f(1) - 1) + f^{′}(1)(2g(1) + 1) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot (2 - 1) + 2 \\cdot (2 \\cdot (-1) + 1) \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100663 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "a87386d5-4a1b-539c-aeb9-dd60181baa4f" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-6154" :question/problem "The values of functions $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $p(x)$ | $q(x)$ | $p'(x)$ | $q'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $8$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(p(x) + 5q(x) \\big)$ at $x=-3$." :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(p(x) + 5q(x) \\right) = p'(x) + 5q'(x)\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(p(x) + 5q(x)) \\mid _{x =-3} &= p^{′}(-3) + 5q^{′}(-3) \\\\\n&= 0 + 5 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&=-10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100664 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "d1d0a3ec-2a84-580a-968e-53b773510853" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-6155" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big)$ at $x=0$." :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big) = f(x)g'(x)+f'(x)g(x)\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(f(x)g(x)) \\mid _{x = 0} &= f(0)g^{′}(0) + f^{′}(0)g(0) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 0 + 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&=-6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f94bf62-9274-5244-84de-a081988a8cd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15-2{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246609} {:answer/id #uuid "4913b668-1754-54cc-96ea-c9f8b3a530ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246610} {:answer/id #uuid "30d2b2ee-93e1-5fa6-90e8-6697f0333aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246611} {:answer/id #uuid "205f05f7-f7ce-59fb-8d8c-60c68f5c7f15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246612} {:answer/id #uuid "a4fdd6ad-7b92-527c-ac87-e79e74e01dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4fdd6ad-7b92-527c-ac87-e79e74e01dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246613} :answer-field/id #uuid "728bb5f9-6597-5709-91f1-7094f3f21c38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246608}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "511629c4-2274-5269-a07e-e24b1312924b" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-104446" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $2\\pi $ | $-3$ | $\\pi $ | $5$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=4.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))=f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=4} & =f(4){g}^{′}(4)+g(4){f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =7\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1ed2777-dec8-5b25-bd45-b8e535b275fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246616} {:answer/id #uuid "5a8bc6a0-bab2-57f3-9783-ec74f1b548a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246617} {:answer/id #uuid "a9be5419-7ebd-504a-ab34-ddf52d3527eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246618} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e1c6d8-657b-5224-acdf-2b634a37ebe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246619} {:answer/id #uuid "10ee1fe6-574e-51a8-a085-1e953bb6d17f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1ed2777-dec8-5b25-bd45-b8e535b275fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246616} :answer-field/id #uuid "b69260a8-2622-5cdc-a168-7709a5cba35e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246615}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08f3cd0f-3528-5f25-b102-19fb21d47d50" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-104447" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(-7)=2\\sqrt{3},\\,{f}^{′}(-7)=\\sqrt{3},\\,g(-7)=5\\sqrt{3}\\,{g}^{′}(-7)=-4\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=-7.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))=f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-7,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=-7} & =f(-7){g}^{′}(-7)+g(-7){f}^{′}(-7) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-4\\sqrt{3})+5\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a2d7fff-ee22-5bda-b3bc-5479a9d3d607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246623} {:answer/id #uuid "76555765-d0a4-5a7d-ba2a-b9a1d9c35409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246624} {:answer/id #uuid "d59ea303-3570-5d16-aa86-89e6db3bb976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246625} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d73555-63cb-53a1-918d-989a72b23478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246626} {:answer/id #uuid "9eb6dbb4-8cd0-576c-944f-52b54e560f77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d59ea303-3570-5d16-aa86-89e6db3bb976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246625} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b11775-97c9-5801-ad87-998b790fe311" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246622}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bf539ba-a0d5-52e6-be48-e448cdf40953" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-104453" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-6$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-6$ | $-2\\pi $ | $3\\pi $ | $5$ | $-2$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)+2g(x))$ at $x=-6.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)+2g(x))={f}^{′}(x)+2{g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-6$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)+2g(x))|}_{x=-6} & ={f}^{′}(-6)+2{g}^{′}(-6) \\\\  & =5+2(-2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "527ff5dc-d845-52dc-a3ab-9a86a6a4e06f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246630} {:answer/id #uuid "27e3fd03-2000-5bbd-bc57-8253fdf1598e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246631} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba588c6-fda2-51c0-82c1-63565193eb48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246632} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9eb39e-c6bc-55b9-99e2-56b4c1920082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246633} {:answer/id #uuid "8393f458-7c89-5c21-be38-923e0259cf3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8393f458-7c89-5c21-be38-923e0259cf3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246634} :answer-field/id #uuid "11749645-cd25-5b83-8798-7dddfdfae40c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246629}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a79366df-e0b9-5d49-bb7e-5065998cbac9" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-104769" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(4)=-2,\\,{f}^{′}(4)=4,\\,g(4)=1,\\,{g}^{′}(4)=0\n$$\n\nIf $h(x)=\\frac{2-3f(x)}{g(x)+1},$ compute ${h}^{′}(4).$" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2-3f(x)$ and $v=g(x)+1.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot (g(x)+1)-(2-3f(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x)}{{(g(x)+1)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{-3{f}^{′}(4)\\cdot (g(4)+1)-(2-3f(4))\\cdot {g}^{′}(4)}{{(g(4)+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 4\\cdot (1+1)-(2-3\\cdot (-2))\\cdot 0}{{(1+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9175c1f-fee8-50d3-a133-f7bec4f1ffd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246637} {:answer/id #uuid "d70e4727-8828-51d0-a69e-4a9d9c7a81ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246638} {:answer/id #uuid "f380171e-1679-5bde-8a45-17b12afafd56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246639} {:answer/id #uuid "f166e1c8-dc38-5f21-bdfa-f2a2ee42abab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246640} {:answer/id #uuid "b90096c8-b0de-56ad-b8eb-2a45c3067364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f380171e-1679-5bde-8a45-17b12afafd56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246639} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee00e16e-271c-58ab-96a3-07382897b36a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246636}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3240a66-403d-59ad-bdc1-5b150e50a8b8" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-105324" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2\\pi $ | $\\pi $ | $\\pi $ | $0$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{(g(0))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\cdot \\pi -2\\pi \\cdot 0}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246642 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "715b4eb6-448a-5bb9-bdf2-2a18a2e27350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246644} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf5760d-72c2-5cc2-b7fb-8b75c17a9d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246645} {:answer/id #uuid "9e5685bb-de5e-5e14-bc0a-2f65cf92737c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246646} {:answer/id #uuid "2196d4ed-be9a-5cb7-a0ba-bf90332869b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246647} {:answer/id #uuid "5a5ed316-0f27-57c2-ae30-9a86e0bbcb6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "715b4eb6-448a-5bb9-bdf2-2a18a2e27350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246644} :answer-field/id #uuid "48fb734f-f5b3-5cbe-9a3b-da55d207dddf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246643}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d8ae87b-0556-525c-9089-eacb2f84dc18" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-105495" :question/problem "For the functions $p(x)$ and $q(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\np(10)=-1,\\,{p}^{′}(10)=-2,\\,q(10)=2,\\,{q}^{′}(10)=1\n$$\n\nIf $z(x)=(2p(x)+q(x))(2-p(x))$, compute ${z}^{′}(10).$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(uv)=u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2p(x)+q(x)$ and $v=2-p(x).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{p}^{′}(x)+{q}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-{p}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}(x) & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(2p(x)+q(x))(-{p}^{′}(x))+(2-p(x))(2{p}^{′}(x)+{q}^{′}(x)) \\\\  & =-{p}^{′}(x)(2p(x)+q(x))+(2{p}^{′}(x)+{q}^{′}(x))(2-p(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=10,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}(10) & =-{p}^{′}(10)(2p(10)+q(10))+(2{p}^{′}(10)+{q}^{′}(10))(2-p(10)) \\\\  & =-(-2)(2(-1)+2)+(2(-2)+1)(2-(-1)) \\\\  & =2(-2+2)-3(2+1) \\\\  & =0-9 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56797035-1680-5d16-8701-3d64a8a8a167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56797035-1680-5d16-8701-3d64a8a8a167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246651} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0130917-fd95-54ff-bf3a-a2a4e772d49c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246650}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32825630-48b0-5a25-9c00-09e9b47eedf4" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-311277" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=5$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $6$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=5.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=5}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=5$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=5} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(5)g(5)-f(5){g}^{′}(5)}{(g(5))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)(-2)-(3)(6)}{(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-18}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203541fa-b636-50ed-90c6-522d061eced1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "203541fa-b636-50ed-90c6-522d061eced1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246654} :answer-field/id #uuid "d670838d-0d21-5c8e-9f04-3376e3fec080" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246653}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1aecccaa-d707-522a-89aa-5451ef41462f" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-340503" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(2)=-1,\\,{f}^{′}(2)=3,\\,g(2)=2,\\,{g}^{′}(2)=-3\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=2.$ \n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x)) & =f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=2} & =f(2){g}^{′}(2)+g(2){f}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed7bb281-eb41-5aa3-9e1c-28289c935272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed7bb281-eb41-5aa3-9e1c-28289c935272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246657} :answer-field/id #uuid "34ba2c5e-4ef9-565d-8f81-e9803ccf4665" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246656}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a336c52-99c0-50c9-8e2c-de3211889702" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-341013" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(4)=2,\\,{f}^{′}(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,g(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,{g}^{′}(4)=-1\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=4.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(4)g(4)-f(4){g}^{′}(4)}{(g(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-2\\cdot (-1)}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+2}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246658 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a204efd-286c-59de-9b0e-333b173f7854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a204efd-286c-59de-9b0e-333b173f7854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246660} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6b651c8-ee74-5b03-85dd-55a61af4303c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246659}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "326e3797-d113-53c3-9a40-8453a755a071" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-341029" :question/problem "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $r(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=1$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $r(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${r}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $5$ | $0$ | $-4$ | $1$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))$ at $x=1.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=1}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))=3{q}^{′}(x)+4{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=1} & =3{q}^{′}(1)+4{r}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =3(-4)+4(1) \\\\  & =-12+4 \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246661 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "842f5648-f3fa-561f-8cbb-e5b79a4a164f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246663} {:answer/id #uuid "6b560c0b-b532-59fe-b558-6c70202f7f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b560c0b-b532-59fe-b558-6c70202f7f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246664} :answer-field/id #uuid "7734e207-60d7-5d5a-95ea-8887ac795f00" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246662}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8399fec-1d8a-543b-b803-9628562e2106" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-341031" :question/problem "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $r(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-1$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $r(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${r}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $-\\sqrt{2}$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))$ at $x=-1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=-1}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))=3{q}^{′}(x)+4{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=-1} & =3{q}^{′}(-1)+4{r}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{2})+4(-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246665 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e60f98a9-4517-54a5-860a-ef3d7d9d27db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e60f98a9-4517-54a5-860a-ef3d7d9d27db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246667} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c1fdac8-14b7-56da-97cf-ff4470bd9d92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246666}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b03c54b8-f199-52e5-91a2-1b985f0b1197" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-341042" :question/problem "For the functions $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nu(4)=1,\\,{u}^{′}(4)=6,\\,v(4)=-2,\\,{v}^{′}(4)=2\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}u(x)+3v(x))$ at $x=4.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}u(x)+3v(x))|}_{x=4}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}u(x)+3v(x))=\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{′}(x)+3{v}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}u(x)+3v(x))|}_{x=4} & =\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{′}(4)+3{v}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(6)+3(2) \\\\  & =3+6 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "755461d9-f3d2-50af-8f70-80ff462b7a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "755461d9-f3d2-50af-8f70-80ff462b7a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246670} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac967da9-243d-53c7-a4d2-b97480f2d0f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246669}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df7e57ca-bb3e-5704-847f-e348f6da28af" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-341450" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $4$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nIf $h(x)=(-2f(x)-3)(g(x)+1),$ find the value of ${h}^{′}(2).$\n\n${h}^{′}(2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Explanation:\n\nThe product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(uv)=u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-2f(x)-3$ and $v=g(x)+1.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =-2{f}^{′}(x)(g(x)+1)+(-2f(x)-3){g}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & =-2{f}^{′}(2)(g(2)+1)+(-2f(2)-3){g}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =-2(2)(-3+1)+(-2(4)-3)(5) \\\\  & =-4(-2)+(-8-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =8+(-11)(5) \\\\  & =8-55 \\\\  & =-47.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45e83aa3-b347-5ffd-80d1-8e6e2462fd1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246673} {:answer/id #uuid "91521d9c-083c-55f6-b869-ac47f3f2247c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45e83aa3-b347-5ffd-80d1-8e6e2462fd1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246673} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4759c2a-ca11-5e5b-99b4-53cd13ae80f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246672}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d2e24374-6397-50d9-a912-6aa8e5601652" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-341468" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(t)$ and $z(t)$ and their derivatives at $t=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2h(t)-5}{1-z(t)},$ compute ${f}^{′}(4).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(4)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2h(t)-5$ and $v=1-z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2{h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-{z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2{h}^{′}(t)(1-z(t))-(2h(t)-5)(-{z}^{′}(t))}{(1-z(t))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt $t=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{2{h}^{′}(4)(1-z(4))-(2h(4)-5)(-{z}^{′}(4))}{(1-z(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(1-(-2))-(2(1)-5)(-1)}{(1-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(3)-(-3)(-1)}{(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18-3}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53a54f0f-91c1-56f1-8a1b-049bb004eac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246677} {:answer/id #uuid "20f12f06-79e0-5747-af5a-7bdc846bae94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246678} {:answer/id #uuid "0573b694-1a10-5eb0-853f-da31d3d2ce6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246679} {:answer/id #uuid "057ff728-0a72-5294-9350-08c0f00f4d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246680} {:answer/id #uuid "e402acff-f8ae-558b-979b-659d9ac5c98d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e402acff-f8ae-558b-979b-659d9ac5c98d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246681} :answer-field/id #uuid "8765e35f-5939-5d58-957d-9d0d711eb610" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246676}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8309ca21-d36c-57be-afb2-430137fc5049" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-48835" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(e)=1,\\,{f}^{′}(e)=\\frac{1}{e},\\,g(e)={e}^{2},\\,{g}^{′}(e)=2e\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=e.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x)) & =f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=e$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=e} & =f(e){g}^{′}(e)+g(e){f}^{′}(e) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2e+{e}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{e} \\\\  & =3e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efaf69f4-fd40-59e3-a2e5-379a571bb8c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246684} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8f987e-40f3-5785-86da-0954ec96c27d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246685} {:answer/id #uuid "f479f571-8f10-566f-ba16-4b3304d706d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246686} {:answer/id #uuid "ea7ddc8c-65aa-5b9d-bc7f-93a35d7d755e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246687} {:answer/id #uuid "76657296-d86a-516f-a1b1-b074c29c7ae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76657296-d86a-516f-a1b1-b074c29c7ae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246688} :answer-field/id #uuid "f55da421-b2d8-58a5-94e9-fbc7d9c9f491" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246683}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a128b3fc-5f71-524e-9a5d-93eeaafef2df" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-48836" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(4)=-3,\\,{f}^{′}(4)=-1,\\,g(4)=2,\\,{g}^{′}(4)=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=4.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x)) & =f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=4} & =f(4){g}^{′}(4)+g(4){f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b3509b-0364-5fa0-a6ea-1b6f4632a646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099697} {:answer/id #uuid "850438ad-51c9-5986-97ef-19a3e767ab64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099698} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe1259c-b6c0-5ac0-adc1-79e776472972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099699} {:answer/id #uuid "decde0ab-bebe-5a15-afa6-992f4cf7299a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099700} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5a2d84-2b1d-51f3-b7b7-396e3ccef9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "decde0ab-bebe-5a15-afa6-992f4cf7299a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099700} :answer-field/id #uuid "750db73d-40a6-5399-8d52-2868fecc4fdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099696}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cd961da-21ad-5bfd-88cf-d61e5f8fe86e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-48844" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you are given the following data:\n\n$f(0) = 2, f^{′}(0) = 2, g(0) = 1, g^{′}(0) = 2$\n\nCompute $\\frac{d}{dx}((f(x))/(g(x)))$ at $x = 0$." :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{{g}^{2}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99e19df1-0a6c-5fcb-9b82-b1420ed3a56c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246691} {:answer/id #uuid "d3774151-642d-50ff-a611-09a1e501b303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246692} {:answer/id #uuid "ad9d0df9-0242-569f-90d3-cd7aa8aa726d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246693} {:answer/id #uuid "e00f5140-fb61-5826-9e77-2f9c1a0e2383" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246694} {:answer/id #uuid "a3833ed9-b538-5ca8-9b39-271367942570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3774151-642d-50ff-a611-09a1e501b303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246692} :answer-field/id #uuid "10d2204a-3a2f-568c-b9b5-6ec7b6c37953" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246690}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71d7b6ec-4bf0-538b-a83d-e6257da5291e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-48960" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=3$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-4$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=3} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(3)g(3)-f(3){g}^{′}(3)}{(g(3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}}{(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fda7ea7f-81c3-5703-9be0-b95fd1af806c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246698} {:answer/id #uuid "6494c263-609b-5eab-998b-dcdf958759ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246699} {:answer/id #uuid "606316ba-eff2-5cc0-a352-a77a27663ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246700} {:answer/id #uuid "02ce33fe-47ed-5c28-8b10-a4965a425ac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246701} {:answer/id #uuid "843793ad-d0d5-5f7c-aacf-6fff8d32bccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "606316ba-eff2-5cc0-a352-a77a27663ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246700} :answer-field/id #uuid "b785d613-bec6-5161-b275-e95ff69862a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246697}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "642e706d-880d-5e53-b334-1d3dda07b034" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-4961" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $t=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $5$ | $8$ | $-3$ | $4$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{1-h(t)}{z(t)},$ compute ${f}^{′}(2).$" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-h(t)$ and $v=z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=-{h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-{h}^{′}(t))\\cdot z(t)-(1-h(t))\\cdot {z}^{′}(t)}{(z(t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-z(t){h}^{′}(t)-{z}^{′}(t)(1-h(t))}{{z}^{2}(t)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=2,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{-z(2){h}^{′}(2)-{z}^{′}(2)(1-h(2))}{{z}^{2}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\cdot (-3)-4\\cdot (1-5)}{{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24+16}{64} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e41d8c9-8103-5f6f-a520-067ce87c9214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246705} {:answer/id #uuid "27bb7dfa-cb16-5f79-afc6-2b80978f1928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246706} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d69288-45e5-5707-b74f-a036137474df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246707} {:answer/id #uuid "735315bb-6f83-5e6c-8bd4-59ec24e1d9d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246708} {:answer/id #uuid "3295f48a-b511-5813-858b-ec2bd2d15d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "735315bb-6f83-5e6c-8bd4-59ec24e1d9d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246708} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d00275a-e166-5efa-8371-b33cad48d7d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246704}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "230d486d-661d-580f-9003-d08606129412" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-72992" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $p(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(-3)=-6,\\,{f}^{′}(-3)=2,\\,p(-3)=-5,\\,{p}^{′}(-3)=-3\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)+p(x))$ at $x=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)+p(x))={f}^{′}(x)+{p}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)+p(x))|}_{x=-3} & ={f}^{′}(-3)+{p}^{′}(-3) \\\\  & =2+(-3) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
